<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gojeb River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gojeb is a river of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, a tributary of the Omo. Rising in the western highlands, it flows east through forested country and long formed the northern boundary of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/feodosia">Kaffa</a>, separating it from the Gibe kingdoms such as Jimma, and the frontier of Dawro to the south-east.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gojeb-river.jpg" alt="Gojeb River" width="320" height="353" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Braxmeier &amp; Peter in s, Location map:NordNordWest · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Omo_OSM.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
